---
description: Hot-path performance rules for prediction and training code
globs:
  - "src/**"
alwaysApply: false
---

`/predict/bulk/strict` sits on the EPP scheduling critical path: the EPP's Go
coalescing proxy batches concurrent per-pod prediction calls (~1ms window) into
one bulk request, and each prediction replica must sustain ~300 QPS.

- Keep the `predict_batch_fast` fast path fast: `np.fromiter` column extraction,
  dict-of-numpy-arrays DataFrame construction (never per-row list-of-dicts on
  the hot path), no per-request Pydantic `.dict()` conversion, no re-validation
  after ingest.
- Responses on bulk endpoints use `ORJSONResponse` with plain dicts — do not
  reintroduce per-item Pydantic model construction there.
- Lock discipline: snapshot model references under the lock; run DataFrame
  construction and model inference outside it. `load_models()` deserializes
  outside the lock and swaps pointers inside it.
- Ensemble batches are split by queue regime with numpy index arrays and
  predicted per-regime in one shot — preserve this instead of per-row dispatch.
- Model reloads are checksum-guarded; avoid adding per-request filesystem or
  network calls.
- When claiming a performance win, state the measurement method (e.g.
  `tests/test_dual_server_client.py` load client, or `python -m timeit` on the
  feature-prep path) and the before/after numbers.
